<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="008" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Owner-approved role edits and assignment, with the union re-verify</title>
    <phase>0 Foundations</phase>
    <gate>007 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Security role changes on the tables whose append-only and visibility guarantees the project rests on.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-sensitive privilege edits; the union across every role must be judged, not just the edited role.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>L</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>007</deps>
    <tags>dataverse,security,roles,verification</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Apply exactly the role edits the owner approved on 2026-10-07 (D-14, D-18, D-22, D-29, and D-33's three), assign the administrator role to the owner's account, add the five ontology tables read-only to Spaarke Platform, and re-run task 002's union check.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Security fails closed; add only what was approved and prove nothing else moved.</role>
  <goal>Each approved privilege is present on every business-unit copy of the named role, nothing else changed, the union check is recorded, and the owner's spaarkedev1 user holds Spaarke Ontology Administrator.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Owner decisions 2026-10-07 (spec section 9). D-29: the writer gets AppendTo on sprk_communication, sprk_event, sprk_todo and sprk_workassignment (closes task 030's F26: creating a Signal whose subject is a communication fails with AppendToAccess, and the Do-lane subjects would fail the same way). D-18: the writer gets Create on sprk_budgetrevision so the commit route can record Revise budget. D-14: Spaarke Ontology Administrator gets Write on sprk_policyversion so publishing stamps the old version's sprk_inforceto. D-22: Spaarke Ontology Administrator gets Create, Write and Read on sprk_triagecategory (it holds no privilege on that table today), the role is assigned to the owner's account, and the five tables go into Spaarke Platform read-only. D-17's removal of Console User Write on sprk_signal is NOT in this task: it waits until the BFF closes Signals (task 049).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/tasks/002-privilege-reverify-after-column-adds.poml</file>
      <file role="modify">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/security-roles.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner">Scope (D-29): add prvAppendTosprk_Communication, prvAppendTosprk_Event, prvAppendTosprk_Todo and prvAppendTosprk_WorkAssignment to Spaarke Ontology Service. Use ORGANIZATION depth, not Deep: once the writer sits in a customer child BU (#1094), Deep would not reach Secure-team-owned subjects in the sibling Secure Record BU (notes/secure-signals-scoping.md section 4.2). Record the depth.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">Scope (D-18): add prvCreatesprk_BudgetRevision to Spaarke Ontology Service. Do NOT add Write or Delete on sprk_budgetrevision, and do NOT add any privilege on sprk_budget (which identity updates the budget amount is undecided, spec section 11.1 O-16).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">Scope (D-14): add prvWritesprk_PolicyVersion to Spaarke Ontology Administrator only. No other role gains it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">Scope (D-22): add Create, Write and Read on sprk_triagecategory to Spaarke Ontology Administrator only. sprk_triagecategory is organisation-owned; use organisation depth and record it. Assign Spaarke Ontology Administrator to the owner's spaarkedev1 user (ask the owner for the exact user if it is not unambiguous from systemuser).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">Scope (D-22): add sprk_signal, sprk_decisionrecord, sprk_policy, sprk_policyversion and sprk_budgetrevision to the Spaarke Platform model-driven app for inspection, with forms that are read-only (a form or field setting, no plugin, ADR-002). Check spec section 8.1 first: the owner may already have done part of this.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">AMENDED 2026-10-07 (D-33): three more edits, owner-approved. (a) Secure Record Owner: prvReadsprk_Signal and prvReadsprk_DecisionRecord at User (Basic) depth, matching its other codified child tables; BEFORE applying, the live refusal for each table (an assign of a row to the Secure Record Owners team fails with 0x80040299 Read Privilege Check For Owner) must be recorded per config/secure-record-owner-role.json's howToExtend: by task 079 if it has run, otherwise here, and handed to 079. (b) Spaarke Basic User (the role BU default teams hold): prvReadsprk_Signal and prvReadsprk_DecisionRecord at Basic depth, so unsecuring a matter can release its children to the default team. (c) Spaarke Ontology Service: prvAssignsprk_DecisionRecord at Organization depth, which changes a ledger row's OWNER only; Write and Delete on sprk_decisionrecord stay absent from every Spaarke role.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">AMENDED 2026-10-07 (D-33 deploy order): in every environment these role edits land BEFORE any BFF build carrying the new secure-child config (task 039). Otherwise the NFR-05 census clause 5 goes red and every Secure-matter create fails with 0x80040299. Record, per environment, the date applied; task 039 re-runs scripts/Set-SecureRecordOwnerRolePrivileges.ps1 -Verify against the new config.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: edit ALL business-unit copies of each role (task 002 constraint: a top-1 read returns an arbitrary copy). Do not touch Service Writer or Service Deleter.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: do NOT remove prvWritesprk_Signal from Spaarke Console User here (task 049 does it after the BFF closes Signals). Do NOT add any privilege not listed above.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: after the edits, repeat task 002's union check: every role holding Write or Delete on sprk_decisionrecord, or Write on sprk_policyversion, classified as platform, admin, human or Spaarke identity. prvWritesprk_DecisionRecord and prvDeletesprk_DecisionRecord must remain absent from all three Spaarke Ontology roles and from Spaarke Console User.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">COORDINATION WITH uac-r2 (owner 2026-10-07): (1) Before starting, fetch origin/master and re-read the current uac-r2 implementation this task depends on, and name the files (with commit) in the completion record: SecureChildLineage.cs, config/secure-record-owner-role.json, RecordOwnershipResolver (I-6), RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter, CallerRecordAccessProbe, tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Ledger.cs, ADR-034 and its amendments, ExternalCallerContext (ADR-003). (2) Check uac-r2's open PRs and active work for overlap (gh pr list --state open; the uac-r2 current-task.md and TASK-INDEX in C:\code_files\spaarke-wt-unified-access-control-r2 if present) and run /conflict-check. (3) Reuse uac-r2's mechanisms; never build a parallel one. Any change to uac-r2-owned files (the lineage list, the owner-role config, the ledger) goes through uac-r2's review, with the PR linked in this task. (4) If the uac-r2 code has changed in a way that invalidates this plan, STOP and escalate rather than adapting silently.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Dataverse security roles and privileges</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-002-thin-plugins.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/security-roles.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/030-signal-writer-progress.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/spec.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Union privilege check" location="projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/security-roles.md">Sections 6, 7 and 9 record the method, the per-BU-copy artifact and its Core User control.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare the rigor level and reason per root CLAUDE.md section 8, then load the knowledge files above.</step>
    <step order="1">Record the before state: every BU copy of Spaarke Ontology Service, Spaarke Ontology Administrator and Spaarke Console User, with their privileges on sprk_communication, sprk_event, sprk_todo, sprk_workassignment, sprk_budgetrevision, sprk_policyversion, sprk_triagecategory and sprk_signal.</step>
    <step order="2">Apply the D-29 and D-18 edits to Spaarke Ontology Service.</step>
    <step order="3">Apply the D-14 and D-22 edits to Spaarke Ontology Administrator and assign it to the owner's user.</step>
    <step order="3a">D-33: confirm the two live refusals are recorded (079, or record them now), then apply Secure Record Owner Read on sprk_signal and sprk_decisionrecord, Spaarke Basic User Basic Read on both, and Ontology Service Assign on sprk_decisionrecord.</step>
    <step order="4">Add the five tables to Spaarke Platform with read-only forms; publish the app.</step>
    <step order="5">Re-read every BU copy and diff against the before state: only the listed privileges changed.</step>
    <step order="6">Run the union check and the live negative: as a non-admin user holding only the Spaarke roles, an update to a sprk_decisionrecord row is refused.</step>
    <step order="7">Prove the F26 fix live: re-run tests/integration/seam/Signals/SignalWriterSeamTests.cs's communication-subject test as the writer and confirm it passes.</step>
    <step order="8">Append the dated before/after and union result to notes/security-roles.md.</step>
    <step order="9">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task to the completed marker, AND set this POML status element to completed. Both, or scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 fails the next push.</step>
    <step order="10">Record any deviation from this POML in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any human user or any Spaarke application identity ends up holding Write or Delete on sprk_decisionrecord, STOP and escalate: that breaks the append-only guarantee.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a needed edit is not in the list above (for example Write on sprk_budget for the amount update), STOP and ask the owner; do not add it.</trigger>
    <trigger>COORDINATION WITH uac-r2 (owner 2026-10-07): if, on re-reading origin/master, the uac-r2 code this task depends on (record access, ownership, secure children, grants, the route ledger) has changed in a way that invalidates this task's plan, STOP and escalate rather than adapting silently.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="pwsh">Web API role edits</tool>
    <tool name="dataverse-mcp">Read-only verification queries</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="data">Dataverse: role privileges, role assignment, Spaarke Platform app module</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/security-roles.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given every BU copy of Spaarke Ontology Service, when listed, then AppendTo on sprk_communication, sprk_event, sprk_todo and sprk_workassignment and Create on sprk_budgetrevision are present.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given every BU copy of Spaarke Ontology Administrator, when listed, then Write on sprk_policyversion and Create, Write and Read on sprk_triagecategory are present, and the owner's spaarkedev1 user holds the role.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the before/after diff, when compared, then no privilege other than those listed changed on any role, and Spaarke Console User still holds prvWritesprk_Signal (removed later by task 049).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the union check, when run, then prvWritesprk_DecisionRecord and prvDeletesprk_DecisionRecord are absent from every Spaarke role, and every holder of Write on sprk_policyversion is Spaarke Ontology Administrator or a platform/admin role, classified in the notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: as a non-admin user holding only the Spaarke roles, an update to a sprk_decisionrecord row is refused.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: Spaarke Ontology Service holds no privilege on sprk_budget and no Write or Delete on sprk_budgetrevision.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the writer identity, when the seam test writes a Signal whose subject is a communication, then it succeeds (F26 closed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given every BU copy of Secure Record Owner, Spaarke Basic User and Spaarke Ontology Service, when listed, then Read (Basic) on sprk_signal and sprk_decisionrecord, Read (Basic) on both, and Assign (Organization) on sprk_decisionrecord respectively are present (D-33), and a recorded live refusal exists for each of the two tables from before the Secure Record Owner edit.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: after the D-33 edits, no Spaarke role holds Write or Delete on sprk_decisionrecord; the AppendTo privileges added for D-29 are at Organization depth.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the deploy log, when read, then the role edits are dated before any BFF deploy carrying the secure-child config.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the Spaarke Platform app, when a user opens a sprk_signal or sprk_policyversion form, then it is read-only.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec.md FR-14a (amended, D-33), FR-21 (amended, D-14), FR-52, FR-56, NFR-11; notes/secure-signals-scoping.md sections 4.2-4.4, 5.2. Task 049 removes Console User Write on sprk_signal and re-runs the same union check.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
